WEBVTT

00:15:26.961 --> 00:15:30.124
and if both partners agree to declare war
on their own selfishness,

00:15:30.148 --> 00:15:32.260
then you'll probably have a good marriage.

00:15:32.284 --> 00:15:39.280
CA: I think Alain de Botton has said that
one of the keys in making that decision

00:15:39.304 --> 00:15:41.574
is finding someone where
you can figure out

00:15:41.598 --> 00:15:45.369
how to resolve the inevitable unhappiness

00:15:45.393 --> 00:15:47.587
with each other
that you're going to walk into.

00:15:47.611 --> 00:15:51.498
DB: Right; he has a good line that, before
you're married or living with someone,

00:15:51.522 --> 00:15:54.479
you can live under the illusion
that you're easy to live with.

00:15:54.503 --> 00:15:56.234
And once you're living with someone,

00:15:56.258 --> 00:15:58.755
you realize, "Oh, I'm actually
not easy to live with.

00:15:58.779 --> 00:16:01.339
I never shut the drawers.
I don't turn off the lights.